1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:02,224
The world worships the rising sun...

2
00:00:02,224 --> 00:00:04,560
...Chhath honours the setting one too.

3
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:06,298
Why? In the last story,

4
00:00:06,298 --> 00:00:08,305
Surya gave food to Yudhishthira...

5
00:00:08,305 --> 00:00:11,846
...but the secret of the setting sun is hidden in two texts.

6
00:00:11,846 --> 00:00:12,850
The first clue...

7
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:13,731
In the Vedas,

8
00:00:13,731 --> 00:00:17,469
the Taitiriya Aranyaka says that every evening as the sun sets,

9
00:00:17,469 --> 00:00:18,774
Mandeha demons attack.

10
00:00:18,774 --> 00:00:20,910
Sages chant Gayatri and offer water.

11
00:00:20,890 --> 00:00:24,316
That water becomes a thunderbolt and demons flee.

12
00:00:24,316 --> 00:00:26,972
Meaning... Arghya is not just worship,

13
00:00:26,972 --> 00:00:28,860
it protects the sun. But...

14
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:30,668
The Vedas don't stop there.

15
00:00:30,668 --> 00:00:35,980
It says whoever meditates on both the rising and setting sun receives every blessing.

16
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:39,371
That same sound echoed during another war.

17
00:00:39,371 --> 00:00:41,496
The second clue is in the Ramayana,

18
00:00:41,496 --> 00:00:43,500
during the weary battle of Lanka.

19
00:00:43,610 --> 00:00:44,865
...sunk in worry.

20
00:00:44,865 --> 00:00:47,670
Then Sage Agastya came... ...and said:

21
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:49,612
[Agastya] Ram,

22
00:00:49,612 --> 00:00:51,266
listen to this Aditya Hridaya.

23
00:00:51,266 --> 00:00:54,630
Chanting it ensures victory and reveals Chhath's true secret.

24
00:00:54,350 --> 00:00:54,592
[Sanskrit] Salutations to the mountain of the east,

25
00:00:54,592 --> 00:00:54,800
and salutations to the mountain of the west.

26
00:00:55,190 --> 00:01:00,752
Salutations to the rising sun on the eastern mountain and to the setting sun on the west.

27
00:01:00,752 --> 00:01:02,690
Ram watched and chanted thrice.

28
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:05,380
and his worry vanished. Then,

29
00:01:05,380 --> 00:01:07,740
in that same war, Ravan fell.

30
00:01:09,710 --> 00:01:11,368
You must have got the answer,

31
00:01:11,368 --> 00:01:15,598
both Vedas and Ramayana respect the setting sun as much as the rising one.

32
00:01:15,598 --> 00:01:17,770
The name Chhath is not in these texts,

33
00:01:17,890 --> 00:01:21,793
That is why Chhath honors both the setting and rising sun.

34
00:01:21,793 --> 00:01:23,139
We salute good days,

35
00:01:23,139 --> 00:01:25,360
but what when they begin to fade?

36
00:01:25,470 --> 00:01:26,997
then the mind turns away.

37
00:01:26,997 --> 00:01:29,562
Chhath does the exact opposite. In Chhath,

38
00:01:29,562 --> 00:01:32,433
devotees first offer Arghya to the setting sun,

39
00:01:32,433 --> 00:01:33,960
then wait the whole night

40
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:36,418
and in the morning to the rising sun.

41
00:01:36,418 --> 00:01:37,884
Meaning Chhath teaches,

42
00:01:37,884 --> 00:01:39,924
a declining day is not a defeat,

43
00:01:39,924 --> 00:01:41,900
it is a promise of the morning.

44
00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:44,308
Therefore, bow to bad days too,

45
00:01:44,308 --> 00:01:46,130
they lead you to the morning.

46
00:01:46,130 --> 00:01:47,450
Try doing this today,

47
00:01:47,670 --> 00:01:50,064
Pause as the sun sets and thank the day,

48
00:01:50,064 --> 00:01:51,021
whatever it was.

49
00:01:51,021 --> 00:01:53,295
Because the world worships the rising,

50
00:01:53,295 --> 00:01:55,390
but morning comes from the setting.

51
00:01:55,850 --> 00:01:57,889
Send this story to your loved ones,

52
00:01:57,889 --> 00:02:00,860
maybe it will help someone in their declining days.

53
00:02:00,860 --> 00:02:01,617
Next story...

54
00:02:01,617 --> 00:02:04,180
Arjun was trembling and Krishna was smiling.

55
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:04,760
Why?

